# Implementation Plan: User Authentication (Login / Signup) & State Management

This plan details the design and step-by-step implementation for adding user authentication (Sign Up, Log In, Session Persistence, and Route Protection) with React Context state management and Express JWT/bcrypt backend.

---

## 1. Architectural Overview

```text
                                 [ BROWSER ]
                                      │
              ┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐
              ▼                                               ▼
     Unauthenticated User                            Authenticated User
  (Browse Home, Login, Signup)                 (Analyze, Dashboard, History, Profile)
              │                                               │
              └───────────────► [ AuthContext ] ◄─────────────┘
                                (React Context)
                                  ├─ user: { id, name, email }
                                  ├─ token: JWT (in localStorage)
                                  ├─ login(email, password)
                                  ├─ register(name, email, password)
                                  └─ logout()
                                      │
                                      ▼
                             [ Axios Interceptor ]
                      (Attaches `Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
                                      │
                                      ▼ HTTP /api/auth/*
                             [ Express Backend ]
                                      │
              ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐
              ▼                       ▼                       ▼
     POST /api/auth/register    POST /api/auth/login    GET /api/auth/me
              │                       │                       │
              └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘
                                      ▼
                            [ User Model (Mongoose) ]
                           (bcrypt password hashing)
                                      ▼
                            [ MongoDB (users coll) ]
```

---

## 2. User Review & Decisions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Guest vs. Protected Analysis Policy**:
> We can support either:
> 1. **Hybrid/Optional Mode (Recommended)**: Visitors can still test the demo and analyze a leaf without signing in (stored as anonymous), while signed-in users have their scans tied to their account so their history and analytics are personal.
> 2. **Strict Mode**: Leaf analysis, history, and dashboard require signing in first.
> *In our proposed plan, we implement the Protected Route architecture while keeping the backend flexible (optional auth supported on analyze, protected on user profile).*

